- Description: Create an alert with title, description, and optional coordinates and verify that the response contains the required fields.
- Action: Send POST /alerts with JSON body {"title": "Suspicious activity near the park", "description": "A person looking into cars on Maple Street.", "latitude": 37.7749, "longitude": -122.4194}
- Expected behavior: Status code 201. Response body is a JSON object that includes "id" (non-empty string), "title" equal to the input title, "description" equal to the input description, and "city" (a non-empty string).

- Description: Create an alert without coordinates and verify that the response still contains a city string.
- Action: Send POST /alerts with JSON body {"title": "Noisy construction", "description": "Loud drilling at 2 AM."}
- Expected behavior: Status code 201. Response body includes "id" (non-empty string), "title" equal to input title, "description" equal to input description, and "city" present as a string (may be empty or any value).

- Description: Submit an alert with an invalid latitude type (string instead of number).
- Action: Send POST /alerts with JSON body {"title": "Invalid coord", "description": "Bad latitude", "latitude": "not-a-number", "longitude": 20.0}
- Expected behavior: Status code 4xx (may be 400 or 422).

- Description: Submit an alert with both required fields omitted.
- Action: Send POST /alerts with JSON body {"latitude": 10.0, "longitude": 20.0}
- Expected behavior: Status code 4xx.

header_code:
import requests

from scenarios.base import AppInstance


def post_alert(app: AppInstance, payload: dict) -> requests.Response:
    url = f"http://localhost:{app.port}/alerts"
    return requests.post(url, json=payload)


def get_alert(app: AppInstance, alert_id: str) -> requests.Response:
    url = f"http://localhost:{app.port}/alerts/{alert_id}"
    return requests.get(url)


def is_client_error(status_code: int) -> bool:
    return 400 <= status_code < 500

